course: dictionary
lesson: 7283
title: Words ending in -ish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The ending -ish means "a bit" or "roughly". Pinkish means slightly pink: a colour with a little pink in it.
explain: «Inside you stands a frame of 206 bones, and they are not dry and dead like a museum skeleton: living bone is wet, pinkish, full of blood vessels, and grows and mends itself.» Pinkish tells you the bone is not fully pink, only a little pink, and it is a soft, living colour.
explain: Look for the pattern. Reddish is a bit red, tallish is a bit tall, and sevenish is roughly seven. Ask: does the word mean "a bit of" the word it came from? If it does, the -ish ending is doing its job.
fact: The ending -ish means a bit or roughly.
fact: «Pinkish» means slightly pink.
fact: Other examples: «reddish» means a bit red, «tallish» means a bit tall, and «sevenish» means roughly seven.
fact: Writers use pinkish to describe things like a pinkish sky at sunset or pinkish flowers.
fact: A good check is to swap in "a bit pink" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The sky turned pinkish as the sun went down.» What does pinkish mean? | Loud and bright | Wet and cold | Very dark and black | *Slightly pink
exercise: The word «tallish» is made from tall and -ish. What does it mean? | Very tall, the tallest of all | Tall and thin | *A bit tall, or roughly tall | Not tall at all
exercise: Which word means roughly seven? | *Sevenish | Sevenfold | Seventh | Sevens
test: «Inside you stands a frame of 206 bones, and they are not dry and dead like a museum skeleton: living bone is wet, pinkish, full of blood vessels.» In this sentence, what does pinkish describe? | A dry museum skeleton | *Living bone | A bunch of flowers | The sky at sunset
test: Which word means a bit blue? | Bluest | *Bluish | Blue-black | Blueness
exam: What does the ending -ish add to a word like pink? | Stronger, the most pink of all | A question mark | *A bit, or roughly | Nothing, it is a different colour
